			<div class="content" id="post-content-4857696">
									

<p>(Zyn, do you just lurk on the Recent Posts page and leap in with relevant links/info when you see somebody asking for help, like a superhero with extremely specific priorities?)</p>
<p>Creidieki, one issue is that a lot of Foundation lore is ambiguous, and is interpreted different ways by different authors. &quot;Does the black moon howl?&quot; has been used as a motto, a passcode prompt, a key concept in <a href="/tanhony-s-proposal-ii">an SCP-001 entry</a>, and many more besides. The only real common thread is that it's spooky and mysterious, and somehow associated with the Foundation. Having a clear reference for this sort of thing can be a bit tricky!</p>
<p>I tried to write this article such that even if you're not super familiar with Foundation lore, you can pick up enough from context clues to get the gist. The Ethics Committee is exactly what it says on the tin, for example. <sup>or is it?</sup><sub>probably</sub><sup>hmmm</sup><sub>don't worry about it.</sub></p>
<p>Anyway, the Foundation can be pretty lore-dense sometimes, but I hope you still enjoyed the article!</p>

							</div>

								
					
